QNX's setlocale() names the default locale "C;ctype:POSIX"; locale.getlocale() raises ValueError on it and every pcap_open_live() (sniffing with a filter) failed while decoding libpcap's empty error text. Fall back to UTF-8.

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific

--- a/scapy/utils.py
+++ b/scapy/utils.py
@@ -914,7 +914,13 @@
     Decode bytes into a string using the system locale.
     Useful on Windows where it can be unusual (e.g. cp1252)
     """
-    return x.decode(encoding=locale.getlocale()[1] or "utf-8", errors="replace")
+    try:
+        enc = locale.getlocale()[1]
+    except ValueError:
+        # QNX: setlocale() names the default locale "C;ctype:POSIX", which
+        # locale.getlocale() cannot parse.
+        enc = None
+    return x.decode(encoding=enc or "utf-8", errors="replace")
 
 
